        {
          "id": "SP_HALICNEMIA_GENICULATA_SAR_1958",
          "name": "Halicnemia geniculata Sarà, 1958",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Halicnemia",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Small and thin, yellow-ochre encrustation (1 cm 2) on a coralligenous block. Skeleton. Not observed. Spicules. Long tylostyles, 405 (1351.7) 1976 x 1.5 (2.7) 4 μm, generally straight, with terminal or subterminal swellings variable in shape; irregular and polytylote forms are to be found (Fig. 13 A). Rabdhotylostyles with heads as above, 147 (242) 705 x 1.5 (2.7) 4 μm (Fig. 13 B); oxeas long, sinuous and thin, 460 (757) 1118 x 1.5 (2.5) 5 mm (Fig. 13 C); acanthoxeas slightly curved or bent, uniformly spined, 42.5 (51.8) 62.5 x 1.5 (1.8) 2 μm (Fig. 13 D).",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2250501",
